<li about="#cite_note-10" id="cite_note-10" data-mw-footnote-number="10"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAdo"><a href="#cite_ref-10" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAds"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAdw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-10" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt31" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAd0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.nytimes.com/2009/12/11/education/11toulmin.html"},"title":{"wt":"Stephen Toulmin, a Philosopher and Educator, Dies at 87"},"last":{"wt":"Grimes"},"first":{"wt":"William"},"date":{"wt":"11 December 2009"},"newspaper":{"wt":"[[The New York Times]]"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFGrimes2009" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt31">Grimes, William (11 December 2009). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2009/12/11/education/11toulmin.html" class="external text" id="mwAd4">"Stephen Toulmin, a Philosopher and Educator, Dies at 87"</a>. <i id="mwAd8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwAeA">The New York Times</a></i>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Stephen+Toulmin%2C+a+Philosopher+and+Educator%2C+Dies+at+87&amp;rft.date=2009-12-11&amp;rft.aulast=Grimes&amp;rft.aufirst=William&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2009%2F12%2F11%2Feducation%2F11toulmin.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AStephen+Toulmin" class="Z3988" about="#mwt31" id="mwAeE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-11" id="cite_note-11" data-mw-footnote-number="11"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAeI"><a href="#cite_ref-11" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAeM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAeQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-11" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt36" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAeU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Wheeler"},"first":{"wt":"Kip"},"date":{"wt":"19 October 2010"},"url":{"wt":"http://web.cn.edu/kwheeler/documents/Toulmin.pdf"},"title":{"wt":"Toulmin Model of Argument"},"website":{"wt":"cn.edu"},"access-date":{"wt":"2018-10-12"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFWheeler2010" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt36">Wheeler, Kip (19 October 2010). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://web.cn.edu/kwheeler/documents/Toulmin.pdf" class="external text" id="mwAeY">"Toulmin Model of Argument"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwAec">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwAeg">cn.edu</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwAek">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwAeo">12 October</span> 2018</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=cn.edu&amp;rft.atitle=Toulmin+Model+of+Argument&amp;rft.date=2010-10-19&amp;rft.aulast=Wheeler&amp;rft.aufirst=Kip&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fweb.cn.edu%2Fkwheeler%2Fdocuments%2FToulmin.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AStephen+Toulmin" class="Z3988" about="#mwt36" id="mwAes"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-12" id="cite_note-12" data-mw-footnote-number="12"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAew"><a href="#cite_ref-12" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAe0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAe4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-12" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books/about/Decision_by_Debate.html?id=v4h3dJczRfcC" class="external text" id="mwAe8">Book description of <i id="mwAfA">Decision by Debate</i> at Google Books</a>: "The most lasting legacy of the work is its break with formal, deductive logic and its introduction of Stephen Toulmin's model of argument to undergraduate student debaters, which, since then, has become a mainstay of what many have called the Renaissance of argumentation studies. Without the work presented in <i id="mwAfE">Decision by Debate</i>, contemporary interdisciplinary views of argumentation that now dominate many disciplines might have never have taken place or at least have been severely delayed."</span></li>
